From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Sat, 6 Jun 2026 11:21:07 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: mxl862xx: advertise legacy SerDes phy-modes on old
 firmware

The downstream legacy SFP API fallback wires up the legacy PCS for
firmware older than 1.0.84, but mxl862xx_phylink_get_caps() still gated
every SerDes interface mode behind a 1.0.84 check. On a switch running
older firmware this left the SerDes ports (9 and 13) with an empty
supported_interfaces bitmap, so phylink_create() returned -EINVAL and
the whole switch failed to probe. On the SDG-9000 the CPU port is port 9
(10gbase-r), so this took down every LAN port with it.

Advertise the interface modes the legacy SFP PCS can actually drive
(SGMII, 1000BASEX, 2500BASEX, 10GBASER, USXGMII) regardless of firmware
version. Keep 10GKR and the QSGMII sub-port modes gated on 1.0.84, since
they require the XPCS API that only newer firmware provides.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/mxl862xx/mxl862xx-phylink.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/mxl862xx/mxl862xx-phylink.c
@@ -32,14 +32,18 @@ void mxl862xx_phylink_get_caps(struct ds
 		break;
 	case 9:
 	case 13:
-		if (!MXL862XX_FW_VER_MIN(priv, 1, 0, 84))
-			break;
 		__set_bit(PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_SGMII, config->supported_interfaces);
 		__set_bit(PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_1000BASEX, config->supported_interfaces);
 		__set_bit(PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_2500BASEX, config->supported_interfaces);
 		__set_bit(PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_10GBASER, config->supported_interfaces);
-		__set_bit(PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_10GKR, config->supported_interfaces);
 		__set_bit(PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_USXGMII, config->supported_interfaces);
+		/* 10GKR and the QSGMII sub-port modes need the XPCS API only
+		 * present in firmware >= 1.0.84; the legacy SFP PCS drives the
+		 * modes set above on older firmware.
+		 */
+		if (!MXL862XX_FW_VER_MIN(priv, 1, 0, 84))
+			break;
+		__set_bit(PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_10GKR, config->supported_interfaces);
 		fallthrough;
 	case 10 ... 12:
 	case 14 ... 16:
